# React components

Write every component outside `src/components/ui` as an arrow function typed with `FC`. Put its props on a named interface next to the component. A component with no props uses `FC` alone.

```tsx
import type { FC } from 'react'

interface FeedTableProps {
  rows: Array<FeedItem>
}

export const FeedTable: FC<FeedTableProps> = ({ rows }) => {
  return null
}
```

Leave `src/components/ui` as generated shadcn source. Hooks stay `function` declarations.

Declare a route component before the route option that references it. Read that route with `getRouteApi`, because an arrow component is not hoisted.
